{
  "configuration_id": "config_016",
  "reason": "With only one data point (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 at 48.5% acc), the largest source of uncertainty is whether the image modality contributes any signal. Config_016 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat) is the minimal-change extension of config_001: it keeps the same RNA encoder and profile setting and only adds an image branch with simple concatenation. This directly isolates the effect of adding image information. If accuracy improves meaningfully, it justifies investing remaining budget in richer multimodal configurations (ViT, multiprofile, transformer aggregation, weighted fusion). If it does not, it redirects effort toward RNA encoder selection (scvi, scgpt) and profile/aggregation choices. This is the highest-information experiment available because it resolves the single most consequential structural question—whether multimodal fusion is worth pursuing—while changing only one design axis relative to the baseline."
}

